factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  Reel script states Ramaniranjan was 'ஜோதிடர்' from Kumbakonam; article says he is a Kumbakonam astrologer who also does car sales — minor, but reel_script omits the car sales detail (acceptable), however the caption says 'கும்பகோணத்தில் ஜோதிடம், கார் விற்பனை செய்து வரும்' which matches.
  Reel script says 'சீனிவாசனுக்கு வேலையும் போனது' and 'பிரச்சினைகள் தீராத நிலையில்' — article says Srinivasan lost his job, which is accurate, but the reel_script says the accused 'தர மறுத்துவிட்டார்' while article says he failed to return money after being asked; acceptable.
  Caption says 'பங்குச்சந்தை முதலீடு, நகைகளை விற்ற பணத்தைத் திருப்பிக் கேட்டபோதும்' — article says she sold stock investments and jewellery to try to get the money back, not that the money she sold was what she asked for; this is a garbled, unclear sentence.
  Caption says Srinivasan and Gayathri were defrauded of Rs 56 lakh ('மோசடி செய்யப்பட்டனர்' applied to both), while the article says Gayathri paid the money; the phrasing mixes the couple as victims of the cheating with the amount.
  Reel script/caption omits the fact that the police deputy commissioner who ordered the case was Mathivanan in the reel script (it names Pasupathy and Ranganathan but the reel_script omits the commissioner, which is an omitted detail but not a required fact).
